        "description": "Reads specific paths from a YAML file.\nMore efficient than reading entire files when you only need certain values.\n\nPath is specified as an array of strings, e.g., [\"spec\", \"containers\", \"0\", \"image\"]\n- Keys are strings: [\"metadata\", \"name\"]\n- Array indices are strings: [\"items\", \"0\"]\n- Root (entire file): empty array []\n\nReturns the YAML subtree at each path. Useful for:\n- Checking current values before editing\n- Reading specific configuration values\n- Extracting parts of large YAML files\n\nThe order of the returned values matches the order of paths requested"
